{"output":"I’ll inspect the search code and test setup, add a guard against stale requests, and run the existing tests without changing them or installing dependencies.\n\nThe controller lets every completed request update state. I added a request ID check for results, errors, and loading. Clearing the query also advances the ID, invalidating pending requests. The existing tests don’t cover request races, so I’ll run a temporary inline probe as well.\n\nFixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search can update results, loading, or errors. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, all exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; inline node --input-type=module race probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests changed or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Fixed src/search/controller.ts so only the latest search can update results, loading, or errors. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API unchanged.\n\nVerification passed, all exit 0: npm test, all 4 tests; inline node --input-type=module race probe; git diff --check.\n\nNo tests changed or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":11,"tool_calls":[{"name":"skill","status":"success"},{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-batching-iincv9nu/search-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":362,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-04588050a519d12cbec609d2e8c44011.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nsuite_status=$?\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst old = [{ id: 'old', title: 'Old', url: '/old' }];\nconst current = [{ id: 'new', title: 'New', url: '/new' }];\nfor (const outcome of ['resolve', 'reject']) {\n  for (const phase of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const first = c.search('old');\n    const second = c.search('new');\n    if (phase === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(current); await second; }\n    if (phase === 'cleared') await c.search('  ');\n    const before = c.getState();\n    requests[0][outcome](outcome === 'resolve' ? old : new Error('Stale error'));\n    await first;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), before);\n    if (phase !== 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(current); await second; }\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), phase === 'cleared'\n      ? { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null }\n      : { query: 'new', results: current, loading: false, error: null });\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Race probe passed');\nNODE\nprobe_status=$?\ngit diff --check\n diff_status=$?\ngit diff --stat\ngit diff -- src/search/controller.ts\nprintf '\\nExit codes: tests=%s probe=%s diff-check=%s\\n' \"$suite_status\" \"$probe_status\" \"$diff_status\"\nexit $((suite_status || probe_status || diff_status))","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-batching-iincv9nu/search-1-baseline/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":417,"stdout_bytes":2272,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-01f2ea90a8b02ac0153caa7cb4dc3e39.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":43211,"output_tokens":1097},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":7296,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":11}}
